zig cc rejects --exclude-libs ("error: unsupported linker arg"), so drop the
flag lldb 23 puts on every tool that links the shared liblldb.

Upstream added it in llvm/llvm-project#204710: the driver links lldbHost.a and
lldbUtility.a on top of liblldb.so, so HostInfoBase (and its file-static
g_fields) exists twice. On ELF the executable's symbols win, so liblldb.so's
PLT entry for GetShlibDir() could bind to the executable's never-initialized
copy -> null g_fields -> segfault in pthread_once.

That interposition needs the symbol to be re-exported, which only happens with
LLDB_ENABLE_DYNAMIC_SCRIPTINTERPRETERS=ON (it flips libraries to
CXX_VISIBILITY_PRESET=default and adds GetShlibDir to the version script).
lldb.nix pins that option to false, so liblldb keeps hidden visibility and
binds those references internally -- revisit this patch if it is ever enabled.

diff --git a/lldb/cmake/modules/AddLLDB.cmake b/lldb/cmake/modules/AddLLDB.cmake
--- a/lldb/cmake/modules/AddLLDB.cmake
+++ b/lldb/cmake/modules/AddLLDB.cmake
@@ -497,7 +497,8 @@
 function(lldb_prevent_liblldb_symbol_interposition name)
   if(UNIX AND NOT APPLE)
-    target_link_options(${name} PRIVATE "LINKER:--exclude-libs,ALL")
+    # zig cc cannot pass --exclude-libs; safe while
+    # LLDB_ENABLE_DYNAMIC_SCRIPTINTERPRETERS is OFF (see patch header).
   endif()
 endfunction()
